le for our rook.  \n\nThe **en passant capture P: e5-d4** is very promising:  \n- We remove a central pawn and gain a pawn.  \n- The e5 pawn disappears, but we get a pawn on d4 that White might target.  \n- More importantly, it opens the e-file for our rook from a8 after possible future moves.  \n\nGiven that we are Black and the White pawn just moved two squares (PWT1), taking en passant disrupts White’s center and gains material without weakening our structure excessively.  \n\nAnswer: P: e5-d4'}
